{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "base_motion",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "Planned moves of a robot's mobile base: a drive at one velocity for a time, and a move to a pose near the robot.",
      "The implementer plans and executes each and returns a result; they are distinct from the setpoints a leader streams on the drive_link pairing. base_state reports the base's motion, its odometry, its limits and its rest. The base checks no obstacle: it drives as the goal says, and whatever stands in the way is the caller's to know; base_navigation's goals keep clear of obstacles.",
      "Positions and yaws are in the robot frame of base_state. The goal's frame is the robot frame where the robot stood when the goal was accepted, fixed to the floor for the life of the goal. A position is x, y, z in meters, and its z is 0 in every frame of this contract, as base_state defines a position; a yaw is in radians, counterclockwise seen from above. The durations and timeouts a goal names are on the clock the implementer's instance reads, the simulation clock in a simulation.",
      "Every move keeps each axis of its motion, x and y of its linear velocity and yaw, and the acceleration and deceleration of each, within describe_base's linear_limits and yaw_limits, through base_state's limiter, and comes to rest as base_state brings a base to rest. A differential base, whose range along y is 0 to 0, moves along +X and turns; an omnidirectional base moves in any direction of the floor while it turns. move_base steers by base_state's odometry, so a pose is as exact as that odometry; on a base whose odometry is commanded, the move runs on the velocities the base executes alone.",
      "base_state's limiter executes 0 on an axis commanded below its deadband, so an axis that drive_base commands smaller in magnitude than its deadband does not move. While the robot frame stands outside a move_base goal's tolerances, move_base commands each axis that closes the error of the leg it is on at least at that axis's deadband once the command of the leg before it has come to 0, so a slow move still reaches its target.",
      "drive_base and move_base have the mark `moves_robot`: each MCP server, `peppy node call` and each lease holder asks the daemon (`robot_leases.check_move`) whether it may move the robot before it calls one. Both also have the mark `moves_base` (marks.json5), which the workflow side reads: after a call of one of them, a workflow reads each position in the robot frame again before it passes it. robot_stop's stop ends them. The positions of this contract have no mark `robot_frame`: a workflow gives a target of the base as a literal.",
      "One goal of this contract runs at a time. A goal is checked in this order. It is refused with `rejected` for a value it does not take: a drive_base linear_velocity that lies outside describe_base's linear_limits min_velocity and max_velocity along x or y, a drive_base yaw_rate outside its yaw_limits min_rate and max_rate, a linear_velocity or a position whose z is not 0, a duration or a timeout outside its range, a move_base whose motion describe_base's limits cannot run within 60 s, a tolerance that is not positive, and a number that is not finite. It is refused with `resource_unavailable` while the base's motion sensing is silent, as base_state defines silence; with `precondition_failed` while base_states' mode is not standing or moving, the message naming the mode and what brings the base to standing; with `leader_streaming` while the leader of drive_link streams, as drive_link defines it; and with `precondition_failed` while another goal of this contract runs, while the base comes to rest from an earlier goal of this contract, and while another goal of the implementer holds the base, as drive_link defines that hold. The message of a refusal names its cause and what to do.",
      "A goal ends early when its caller cancels it or is gone, and when robot_stop's stop ends it: it then ends cancelled, with a reason that names the cause. Such a goal brings the base to rest and ends once the base rests, or once its settle_timeout_s has passed since the cancel or the stop, whichever comes first; its result gives where the robot frame stood then. A goal fails with `resource_unavailable` when the base's motion sensing falls silent, when its odometry starts over, and when the implementer's clock goes back, the base coming to rest. A goal fails with `attempt_failed` when base_states' mode leaves standing and moving, as when a walking base falls, the message naming the mode; the base's command is then 0, and the mode says what the base does. A goal fails with `attempt_failed` when it cannot go on for another reason. A failed goal gives no result.",
    ],
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    leader_streaming: "A leader of drive_link drives the base",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "drive_base",
        description: "Drive the base at one velocity for a time, then bring it to rest. base_state's limiter moves the command toward the velocity, holds it for hold_duration_s from the step at which the command reaches it, then brings the base to rest. The goal completes once the base rests, as base_state defines rest, and fails with `timeout` when the base does not rest by settle_timeout_s after the command reaches 0; the message gives the base's velocity then. The action gives no feedback. The result gives where the base came to rest in the goal's frame and how long the action took.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            linear_velocity: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "Velocity in the robot frame: x forward, negative to drive backward, y leftward, negative to drive rightward, and z up (m/s); x and y each within describe_base's linear_limits min_velocity and max_velocity along its axis, so y is 0 on a differential base, and z is 0." },
            yaw_rate: { $type: "f64", $description: "Turn rate (rad/s), counterclockwise seen from above; within describe_base's yaw_limits min_rate and max_rate." },
            hold_duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long the command holds the velocity once it reaches it (s), above 0 and at most 60." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long (s, 0 to 60) after the command reaches 0 the base may take to rest before the drive fails. Rest reads 0.2 s of base_states, as base_state defines it, so a value below 0.2 s fails the drive unless the base already rests when the command reaches 0." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            final_position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "Where the robot frame's origin stood in the goal's frame when the drive ended: x, y, z (m); at rest, or at the end of its settle timeout after a cancel or a stop." },
            final_yaw: { $type: "f64", $description: "The robot frame's heading in the goal's frame when the drive ended (rad, in (-pi, pi])." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot", "moves_base"],
      },
      {
        name: "move_base",
        description: "Move the robot frame to a pose in the goal's frame and bring the base to rest there: position [1.2, 0, 0] and yaw 0 drive 1.2 m ahead, and position [0, 0, 0] and yaw 1.57 turn a quarter turn to the left. A differential base turns toward the target, drives to it and turns to the target yaw, and turns in place when the target lies within settle_position_tolerance_m of where the robot stood when the goal was accepted; an omnidirectional base drives straight to the target while it turns to the target yaw. While it drives, it turns toward the target again whenever the target's bearing grows past settle_yaw_tolerance_rad or past the implementer's bearing bound, whichever is smaller, and a base whose linear_limits min_velocity along x is below 0 drives backward to a target it has passed. The move completes once, at or after the planned end of its motion, move_base commands 0 on every axis and the base rests with the robot frame within both tolerances of the target, and fails with `timeout` when it does not by settle_timeout_s after the planned end; the message says how far the base stands from the target. The base then rests where it stands either way. Feedback gives what remains of the move. The result gives where the robot frame stood in the goal's frame when the move ended and how long the action took.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "Target position in the goal's frame: x, y, z (m); z is 0." },
            yaw: { $type: "f64", $description: "Target heading in the goal's frame (rad), any finite angle; the base turns the shorter way to it." },
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested duration of the motion (s), 0 to 60; floored at the duration describe_base's limits allow. 0 = fastest." },
            settle_position_tolerance_m: { $type: "f64", $description: "The move completes once the robot frame's origin rests within this distance (m) of the target." },
            settle_yaw_tolerance_rad: { $type: "f64", $description: "The move completes once the robot frame's heading rests within this angle (rad) of the target yaw; pi or more leaves the heading free." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long (s, 0 to 60) after the planned end the base may take to rest within both tolerances before the move fails. With 0 the move fails at its planned end unless the base already rests within both tolerances then." },
          },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "standard",
          message_format: {
            distance_remaining_m: { $type: "f64", $description: "Distance from the robot frame's origin to the target (m)." },
            yaw_remaining_rad: { $type: "f64", $description: "Magnitude of the shorter angle from the robot frame's heading to the target yaw (rad, in [0, pi])." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            final_position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "Where the robot frame's origin stood in the goal's frame when the move ended: x, y, z (m); at rest, or at the end of its settle timeout after a cancel or a stop." },
            final_yaw: { $type: "f64", $description: "The robot frame's heading in the goal's frame when the move ended (rad, in (-pi, pi])." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot", "moves_base"],
      },
    ],
  },
}
